{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Financial Services to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents relative to financial services.","BillNumber":"S2792","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J11","Name":"Joint Committee on Financial Services","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J11","ResponseDate":"2024-05-17T16:26:16.847"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2792/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, May 20, 2024 -- The committee on Financial Services, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 628) of James B. Eldridge, Patricia D. Jehlen and Sal N. DiDomenico for legislation to promote economic mobility through matched savings; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 632) of James B. Eldridge, Liz Miranda, Jack Patrick Lewis, Carmine Lawrence Gentile and other members of the General Court for legislation to establish a Massachusetts public bank; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 692) of Susan L. Moran for legislation to protect consumers engaging with buy now pay later lenders; and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 693) of Susan L. Moran for legislation to  establish a public bank of Massachusetts to support economic development, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2792).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Financial Services be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 628, 632, 692, and 693 relative to financial services .\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J11","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J11"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}